{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, auditing is active for write and attribute-change attempts against /etc/inventory.conf using the key inventory-config.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The exact persistent rule was created and loaded. Final post-restart checks show auditd active and enabled, kernel auditing enabled with no lost events, and the matching live and persistent rules present.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4503737bc18e4be1","cmd-0bee0750cf514280","cmd-509af9a539a34368","cmd-55c854134cbe4703"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Successful changes to /etc/inventory.conf are recorded in the system audit log with key inventory-config.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A successful append changed the file checksum, and direct inspection of /var/log/audit/audit.log showed the corresponding exact-path SYSCALL record with success=yes and key=inventory-config. Successful operation was also exercised after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3b807129cc994282","cmd-b561ed35589b4912","cmd-e63723094883479c","cmd-4dbeddca39334b43"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Unsuccessful attempted changes to /etc/inventory.conf are recorded in the system audit log with key inventory-config.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Writes attempted as nobody were denied without changing the file, and the audit log directly showed exact-path SYSCALL records with success=no, EACCES, and key=inventory-config, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-af2eaa7cbe394d67","cmd-e63723094883479c","cmd-7366699e40e7425e","cmd-705e50e943c24837"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing auditd was a necessary prerequisite because it was absent; creating and loading the rule directly implemented the task. The bounded pre- and post-restart probes and temporary files supported functional and restart verification, and their changes were fully restored or removed. The reboot was required by the provider-wide protocol. Required package and rule changes remained, while /etc/inventory.conf returned to its prepared checksum and metadata. Final observations show healthy package state, no failed services, no unexpected listeners, and no executor-created temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99126a8adf6c4d8b","cmd-4503737bc18e4be1","cmd-0bee0750cf514280","cmd-3b807129cc994282","cmd-af2eaa7cbe394d67","cmd-50d065af08ef43d9","cmd-dd9a0062054742c0","cmd-4dbeddca39334b43","cmd-7366699e40e7425e","cmd-442c17454bf944f1","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct behavioral evidence demonstrates keyed audit records for both successful and denied changes. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle observations, recovered system/audit/file state, and fresh post-restart behavior.","limitations":["The default ausearch queries in cmd-21a36abc27a74ded and cmd-886245ccaae9433e unexpectedly returned no matches. The reason is not established, although direct raw-log inspection and ausearch with an explicit /var/log/audit/audit.log input subsequently showed the required records in cmd-b561ed35589b4912 and cmd-e63723094883479c.","Some audit-command output was bounded or truncated, but the visible records directly cover the exact target path, key, and both success states."]}
